@mqb3gofjzkko7nzx38 Because the examples actually shown in the video are right next to almond orchards, and at many points throughout the year for weeks at a time, the almond orchards get worked on which produces more dust than you would imagine. I live in this area and being too close to an orchard means everything you own gets absolutely blanketed in thick dust overnight, during these periods. These periods coincidentally are also the brightest points in the year. This all means that it would need either automatic cleaning systems, or simply need to be cleaned daily over very long stretches of the canal.

Being that I live here and have dealt with local county workers I believe this cleaning process will be under staffed and ineffective, like many projects done here.

My understanding is that dust exposure like this also leads to a much lesser productive life for solar panels than they would experience in other, less dusty environments(Many places in the desert are less dusty than this region, ironically).

